From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: N-PHY: route the TSSI on rev 7 and later

When the RSSI select picks the TSSI, b43_nphy_rev3_rssi_select() sets the
radio's TX SSI mux only on rev 3-6 (radio 2056). On rev 7 and later
(radio 2057) the mux stays as the radio came up, the TSSI does not reach
the AFE, and TX power control works on a wrong power estimate.

Do what brcmsmac's brcms_phy_wr_tx_mux() does on rev 7 and later: write
the mux of the core, 0x11 with an external PA (0xe/0xc at 2.4/5 GHz with
an internal one, as on 2056), and power up IQTEST_SEL_PU with an external
PA.

On an ASUS RT-AC56U (BCM43217, N-PHY rev 17, radio 2057 rev 14, external
PA) after a power-on, with its PAs enabled: TX power control index 0x30
and power estimate 0x030 without this, 0x50 and 0x150 with it, as after
the vendor driver ran.

Signed-off-by: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -1811,11 +1811,20 @@ static void b43_nphy_rev3_rssi_select(st
 					enum nl80211_band band =
 						b43_current_band(dev->wl);
 
-					if (dev->phy.rev < 7) {
-						if (b43_nphy_ipa(dev))
-							val = (band == NL80211_BAND_5GHZ) ? 0xC : 0xE;
-						else
-							val = 0x11;
+					if (b43_nphy_ipa(dev))
+						val = (band == NL80211_BAND_5GHZ) ? 0xC : 0xE;
+					else
+						val = 0x11;
+					if (dev->phy.rev >= 7) {
+						b43_radio_write(dev, i == 0 ?
+								R2057_TX0_TX_SSI_MUX :
+								R2057_TX1_TX_SSI_MUX,
+								val);
+						if (!b43_nphy_ipa(dev))
+							b43_radio_write(dev,
+									R2057_IQTEST_SEL_PU,
+									0x1);
+					} else {
 						reg = (i == 0) ? B2056_TX0 : B2056_TX1;
 						reg |= B2056_TX_TX_SSI_MUX;
 						b43_radio_write(dev, reg, val);
